------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. WHY tests/run-all.sh IS NOT THIS TASK'S REGRESSION EVIDENCE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

tests/run-all.sh runs a fixed ordered list under `set -euo pipefail`
(run-all.sh:3), so the FIRST failing suite aborts the whole run. Measured this
round rather than inherited: its `tests=()` array holds exactly 61 entries and
this epic's 13 suites occupy positions 49 through 61 — the tail — behind 48
unrelated suites. tests/run-all.ps1 holds 44 entries.

A full `bash tests/run-all.sh` was nevertheless run AS-IS this round (below). It
announced 21 suites and never reached any epic-189-a1 suite: a grep of the entire
captured transcript for all 13 epic suite names returns 0. The aggregate runner
therefore cannot serve as their evidence, and the 25 individual runs above are
the substitute — this feature's established practice since T-006.

