4. NEITHER ABORT IS ATTRIBUTABLE TO T-013
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The controls above are the load-bearing evidence: both aborts reproduce on a
PRISTINE clone with a verified-clean tree at a HEAD that already CONTAINS all of
T-013's commits. A failure that a task caused cannot be reproduced by removing
nothing and changing nothing; these reproduce with the task's work fully present
and no local state at all.

BASH LANE root cause, verified directly this round rather than cited:

  this branch:  tests/turn-first-workflow.tests.sh:290  ->  '## Output Paths And Hashes' \
  origin/main:  same file, same line 290                ->  '## Outputs' \

  $ git log --oneline b085ec76..HEAD -- tests/turn-first-workflow.tests.sh                              -> 0 commits
  $ git log --oneline b085ec76..HEAD -- plugins/sdd-implementation/scripts/validate-implementation-report.sh -> 0 commits

Zero commits on either file since the merge-base, so a merge takes main's version
of both verbatim, with nothing to conflict. This is WFI-005/WFI-017 contract
drift: the template heading was renamed upstream, and both the suite's needle and
the validator were realigned there. The three upstream fixes were checked for
ancestry rather than assumed:

  6b40b6e1  ancestor of origin/main: YES   ancestor of HEAD: NO
  f2687bef  ancestor of origin/main: YES   ancestor of HEAD: NO
  5a9df172  ancestor of origin/main: YES   ancestor of HEAD: NO

  $ git rev-list --left-right --count origin/main...HEAD   ->  172   224
                                                               ^behind ^ahead

172 behind. The human decided to defer the merge to the final phase because
taking main in now would conflict in the four generated `guard_invariants`
enforcement artifacts, both `check-workflow-state` gate scripts (R-10-protected,
agent-uneditable) and the append-only identity ledger. This chain applies nothing
from main and duplicates no upstream hunk, which is the hazard WFI-017 itself
recorded.

PWSH LANE root cause is DIFFERENT IN KIND and is NOT merge-resolvable. The
message is `stage-provenance: task plan hash is stale`: implement-task's
lifecycle appends to tasks.md necessarily diverge the task-review contract's
bound hash, so task-stage provenance structurally cannot stay green during the
implementation phase. It is resolved by the final-phase provenance re-binding,
not by a merge. It reproduced here on a clean clone at HEAD b3b2805e, i.e. with
T-013's own tasks.md `Status:` edit already present and with no uncommitted
change of any kind.

